Thank you to Percona for Percona Server for MongoDB and Percona Backup for
MongoDB, installed from its official repositories at https://repo.percona.com/.
The database engine, replication, backups and point-in-time recovery come from
Percona's open-source work.

OpenEverest (https://openeverest.io), an Apache-2.0 CNCF Sandbox project
originally known as Percona Everest, inspired Karakoram's self-hosted,
provider-based database orchestration: Provider/Instance concepts, version
bundles, topology schemas, backup storages, PITR/restore flows and RBAC.
Karakoram brings that model to Zerops instead of Kubernetes as an independent
implementation; no OpenEverest code or UI is copied into this repository.

The name is an homage: Everest is the highest peak, while Karakoram is the range
that holds K2 and other giants—a nod to OpenEverest and to growing beyond a
single peak, with room for future engines and backends.

